{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/614221-hunter-2ed-request-an-organistaion-section-for-compacts-and-conspiracies","id":614221,"title":"Hunter 2ed request: An organistaion section for Compacts and Conspiracies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-03T16:05:12-07:00","id":614221,"title":"Hunter 2ed request: An organistaion section for Compacts and Conspiracies","content":"I have a humble request for Hunter 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies should have a section on how they're organised. One of the things I always felt was lacking is that Hunter often didn't make me feel that you were members of these awesome organisations. Sometimes I felt a Cell was four dudes with shotguns, and a Conspiracy was four dudes with Shotguns, and magic tricks. Even something simple like<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> The Malleus Maleficarum parashoots in priests who each train locals to form a cell of front line Hunters or a cell providing logical and information support. These cells form an alliance to protect a geographical region under supervision of a bishop. They patrol the streets and deal with everyday monster issues. For larger problems the bishop will call in a Cell of world travelling special forces, who'll take the lead with support from the local hunters.</div>Would, IMO, go a long way to letting me know where my charachter fits into the organisation, and also introduce a ton of potential charachter concepts. In that paragraph alone there's the priest forming/leading a cell. Local hunters. The bishop. The special forces. (Though one day, I <i>will</i> play The Pope)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-05-2015, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T16:42:23-07:00","id":614282,"title":"","content":"I desperately want Hunter groups to actually feel like large organizations with structure and resources. The 1e style of &quot;everyone is an isolated Cell&quot; is tiring and lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T17:51:02-07:00","id":614335,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Conspiracies be stretched... rather thin at times? I mean, not even the MM, for example, has infinite resources I'm sure. <br /> <br /> I bring it up because that may be a reason for the whole isolated cell thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T23:58:48-07:00","id":614656,"title":"","content":"It's a matter of thematic focus.<br /> <br /> You could play a vampire game where the PC is the only vampire in town, that strikes me as a very sensible survival strategy for vampires. But how much time does the book spend talking about it? Not much, because it goes against the thematic focus of Requiem.<br /> <br /> Same here. To me the entire point of having Conspiracies is that they have a different thematic focus to a lone Cell; so while you might get situations where 4 Conspiracy members end up isolated, it's like that one isolated vampire. It logically happens, but the books shouldn't focus on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:13:33-07:00","id":615324,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't really fault them if the 2e core mostly focuses on that Cell style of play with some stuff devoted to the difference when you're part of a Conspiracy. It seems like creating some basic systems for that in the core, then expanding on it in a supplement would work well.<br /> <br /> That said, it's worth looking at Status in Mortal Remains and how Cheiron and TFV both gain Allies that provide them with Backup. This suggests to me very much the idea that they're not quite isolated like they may have been in the original core (I think this is really just a fault of how the 1e games set themselves up with 'gothic isolation' and all that jazz.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:41:25-07:00","id":615398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/614221-hunter-2ed-request-an-organistaion-section-for-compacts-and-conspiracies?p=615324#post615324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't really fault them if the 2e core mostly focuses on that Cell style of play with some stuff devoted to the difference when you're part of a Conspiracy. It seems like creating some basic systems for that in the core, then expanding on it in a supplement would work well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure - writing hooks in the core and then connecting mechancis to those hooks in suppliments is a perfectly good strategy.<br /> <br /> I'd say fluff in the core is more important than basic systems though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/614221-hunter-2ed-request-an-organistaion-section-for-compacts-and-conspiracies?p=615324#post615324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it's worth looking at Status in Mortal Remains and how Cheiron and TFV both gain Allies that provide them with Backup. This suggests to me very much the idea that they're not quite isolated like they may have been in the original core (I think this is really just a fault of how the 1e games set themselves up with 'gothic isolation' and all that jazz.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The books seem a bit inconsistant on that regard, I agree, but I think they end up far more on the isolation side.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T16:10:34-07:00","id":615686,"title":"","content":"I have to concur it sounds like the isolated cell thing may be a case of issues 1e seemed to have. <br /> <br /> Which is to say I think your issues may very well be addressed in the new core fluff wise at least, assuming it doesn't take very much space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key"